#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265922 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ad42806-a1fb-502b-92c9-cc550a2947d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263104} {:answer/id #uuid "3814d838-f67b-5fd0-9cf1-5bd3b8068e17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263506} {:answer/id #uuid "70300fb3-4714-53a0-81a4-d324647570c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263972} {:answer/id #uuid "a40dd9f9-794b-5250-b118-912c1bcea248" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264398} {:answer/id #uuid "c23a5f0c-9b6e-5b61-bcc9-719659fcd17f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264687}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264687} :answer-field/id #uuid "1393e60c-9a9d-558f-82b5-5e2a716a7edd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265276}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5438297a-3242-553b-b76b-9231f3aaa360" :question/math-academy-id "q-130501" :question/problem "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+y &=4 \\\\ x-y &=-10\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation, all the variables are on the left-hand side, and all the constants are on the right-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+y &=4 \\\\ x-y &=-10\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265923 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11874c88-0d8d-5fdc-98e7-8f98e6a3f365" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263162} {:answer/id #uuid "87092bc6-cce8-59e3-97f8-85ea23e9e36d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264169} {:answer/id #uuid "a375bbba-4d73-59f8-98fd-ff55611b114c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264389} {:answer/id #uuid "c344dea9-14a2-5e14-b911-cdb495284357" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264702} {:answer/id #uuid "d761b6a0-7cd7-5ded-a020-ef128be56117" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264877}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264702} :answer-field/id #uuid "e12d11e5-1bfe-5244-a9f3-13036e9bc00f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265641}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d99d7426-520b-5e1d-945d-430bc4355051" :question/math-academy-id "q-130510" :question/problem "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-1 &=4y \\\\ y &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that it’s in the correct order and  both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-4y &=1 \\\\ 0x+y &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265924 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6149c1e3-2adb-5ef4-9f00-d3b2f8ea2b11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263840} {:answer/id #uuid "ae8b8a48-bedd-5065-93e5-a6639b2ed96c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264503} {:answer/id #uuid "b1b9dd15-da63-5ed4-bc90-f1be32942872" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264529} {:answer/id #uuid "b5a71f49-1f77-5bf1-a994-f837b58aa69e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264571} {:answer/id #uuid "c98be70a-8345-5fab-81a8-e8ad07f81f34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264763}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264571} :answer-field/id #uuid "031ee993-209a-598a-9707-1c175f7a4052" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265254}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "cf8957cc-bd4d-53d8-bdac-5e6b1bfee90e" :question/math-academy-id "q-130511" :question/problem "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-5 &=y \\\\ y &=2x+3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that it’s in the correct order and  both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y &=5 \\\\ -2x+y &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265925 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07c2532f-265d-518f-9242-3d66b909f114" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263072} {:answer/id #uuid "543b0987-b8ca-58c6-ba1b-9391f717f671" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263726} {:answer/id #uuid "9b04c073-d7dd-5790-ad72-0a5eca03bf2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264326} {:answer/id #uuid "9d796aff-5533-5fa8-a17b-584c4f6954b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264348} {:answer/id #uuid "bae2913a-0008-5d4d-af2d-d7a90a3b9ab3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264624}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263072} :answer-field/id #uuid "6bf40629-d731-54a2-b026-37276de9ddd4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265430}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9720c969-3638-5f11-8696-12578cb9e2c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-130514" :question/problem "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3 &=y \\\\ 1 &=-2+x\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that it’s in the correct order and  both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}0x+y &=-3 \\\\ x+0y &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265926 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1dcde906-c5fb-5fc0-b6a8-8961649a59ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}10x+25y &=-15 \\\\ 12x+6y &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422754} {:answer/id #uuid "727892e1-58ea-5d36-b86b-82b51a10eb55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+5y &=3 \\\\ 4x+y &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422822} {:answer/id #uuid "a12e8848-d478-59a6-a4bb-c9297a758c18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}10x+25y &=-15 \\\\ 12x+3y &=6\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422866} {:answer/id #uuid "b92215d8-8706-55a2-9e83-085b95ecb6b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}10x+5y &=-15 \\\\ 12x+3y &=6\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422884} {:answer/id #uuid "e1575aa2-a070-55bb-b7a7-08d8f4d81a38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+5y &=15 \\\\ 4x+y &=-6\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422911}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186422822} :answer-field/id #uuid "0929e729-c74a-53df-b186-d608a6e127ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265262}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2e54120f-ad5a-5b0e-97ad-23133523c995" :question/math-academy-id "q-130523" :question/problem "What is the system of equations represented by\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}10 & 25 \\\\ 12 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}15 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The  $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}10x+25y &=15 \\\\ 12x+3y &=-6\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying both equations in the system, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+5y &=3 \\\\ 4x+y &=-2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265927 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bec536f-f8a0-5917-8735-203411ca376c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-4y &=-1 \\\\ x &=3\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263114} {:answer/id #uuid "13808937-e709-5baf-bd70-906d13045e3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-4y &=3 \\\\ x &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263183} {:answer/id #uuid "441d0ffb-ffd6-58ae-a17d-9d7d0730d034" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-4y &=-1 \\\\ y &=3\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263599} {:answer/id #uuid "834d660c-f342-580a-bd90-9491af1021d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3y-4x &=-1 \\\\ y &=3\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264128} {:answer/id #uuid "e782c9a3-4077-58c9-8359-eecbb821497c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-4y &=-3 \\\\ y &=1\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265016}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263599} :answer-field/id #uuid "71665118-325d-5577-b749-fff1dfd7861f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265439}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d26bf48b-80cb-5dd2-a23e-0d3f566745b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-130525" :question/problem "What is the system of equations represented by\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The  $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-4y &=-1 \\\\ 0x+y &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSimplifying both equations in the system, we get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-4y &=-1 \\\\ y &=3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265949 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "270c57e6-7711-5097-a349-a79d2b878209" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 11 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -8 & 8\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263341} {:answer/id #uuid "7bc7509a-b077-596e-b503-a6e0dec66ceb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 11 & 7 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & -8 & 8 \\\\ -6 & 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264069} {:answer/id #uuid "93f14d5b-0eb8-557c-b676-9b24c3845b20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 3 & 7 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & 1 & 8 \\\\ -6 & 4 & -2\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264268} {:answer/id #uuid "d198949b-7b7d-525d-90ed-58049effbe2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 11 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -8 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264830} {:answer/id #uuid "d3dfa2e4-2fa4-5afe-8263-0d061513fed2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}5 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 11 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & 1 & -8\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264845}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264069} :answer-field/id #uuid "c78322e3-d7b3-5c22-973e-05196f97b043" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265596}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c1ae183f-8ede-5abb-98da-0b2fcbb558c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-130633" :question/problem "What is the minor of ${x}_{12}$ in \n$$\n\\displaystyle X=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 11 & 7 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & 1 & -8 & 8 \\\\ -6 & 4 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get the minor of ${x}_{12}$, we remove the $1$st row and $2$nd column:\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{gray}∗} & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{0} & {\\color{gray}∗} & {\\color{gray}∗} \\\\ 3 & {\\color{gray}∗} & 11 & 7 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & {\\color{gray}∗} & -8 & 8 \\\\ -6 & {\\color{gray}∗} & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the minor is \n\n$$\n{M}_{12}=\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 11 & 7 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & -8 & 8 \\\\ -6 & 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265979 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00c6448e-4233-5ae7-870b-9f446f54a05a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}3 & \\sqrt{5} & 8 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 22 & 5 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 3 & 2 & \\frac{5}{2}\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263008} {:answer/id #uuid "11b89648-4bb4-5cb7-ae49-60a938cf8e6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 & -7 & 0 \\\\ 22 & 5 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 3 & 8 \\\\ 7 & 3 & 4 & 2\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263164} {:answer/id #uuid "a165b042-7361-54c1-ae6b-729e098360fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 & -7 & 0 \\\\ 22 & 5 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 3 & 4 & \\frac{5}{2}\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264373} {:answer/id #uuid "d5f5d612-a58c-57b0-bd69-b2f65c367c29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -5 & 3 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 2 & \\frac{5}{2}\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264862} {:answer/id #uuid "dbc89729-2f0a-549b-8335-d4789e732f8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}3 & \\sqrt{5} & 5 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -7 & 0 \\\\ 22 & 5 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 3 & 8\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264913}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264373} :answer-field/id #uuid "26e079f0-97b0-5db9-8745-45c40ce2bb00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265317}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e92be295-8dc5-5c90-8355-ba0b4a005245" :question/math-academy-id "q-130803" :question/problem "Find the minor of  ${e}_{14}$ in  $$\n\\displaystyle E=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & \\sqrt{5} & 5 & 8 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 22 & 5 & -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 3 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 3 & 4 & 2 & \\frac{5}{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get the minor of ${e}_{14}$, we remove the $1$st row and $4$th column:\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{gray}∗} & {\\color{gray}∗} & {\\color{gray}∗} & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{8} & {\\color{gray}∗} \\\\ 1 & 3 & -7 & {\\color{gray}∗} & 0 \\\\ 22 & 5 & -1 & {\\color{gray}∗} & -2 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 3 & {\\color{gray}∗} & 0 \\\\ 7 & 3 & 4 & {\\color{gray}∗} & \\frac{5}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, the minor is\n\n$$\n{M}_{14}=\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 & -7 & 0 \\\\ 22 & 5 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 3 & 4 & \\frac{5}{2}\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265981 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "172ba195-7d64-5887-b92c-1bc55e85e365" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 0 & 8 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 3 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ -5 & 4 & 6 & 13\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263219} {:answer/id #uuid "3081b7b9-8e01-5549-a48d-5b7d771a3987" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}5 & -3 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 8 & 2 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -5 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 3 & -6 & 3\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263412} {:answer/id #uuid "3b5bc744-85a1-5a13-b189-8565a76b18ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}8 & 2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 5 & 0 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 1 & -5 & 4 & 13 \\\\ 7 & 3 & -6 & -18\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263528} {:answer/id #uuid "7cd7ae9d-c2b7-5224-b457-c233081db543" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}8 & 2 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 5 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -5 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 3 & -6 & 3\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264076} {:answer/id #uuid "d4056372-0af9-56bd-b895-5fc6001455b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}5 & -3 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 8 & 2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 5 & 0 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 1 & -5 & 4 & 13\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264846}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #e