table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-1}}</td><td>$-1$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-2}}</td><td>{{field-3}}</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>$x$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$y$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-4}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$7$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$.$</span>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that it is in the correct order and  both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-y &=-5 \\\\ 3x-2y &=7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299617 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ecd663bb-16f1-5a4a-97e3-d46851159337" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298560}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298560} :answer-field/id #uuid "36ce1f5a-b325-52e2-9f07-3f178f4d5d16" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298826} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49df71b6-726a-55cc-86f7-0c48cf214547" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297855}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297855} :answer-field/id #uuid "77fdab80-24ee-538a-8553-301609daf54b" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299043} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d254648-366b-530c-bd81-35dc1b97af74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297744}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297744} :answer-field/id #uuid "97c0456c-1073-56d4-ba69-2aa6c6d0f1ae" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299138} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01a0cf46-9fd3-531f-a687-e8d3cdf64026" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297560}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297560} :answer-field/id #uuid "a1a54e8c-b51c-575e-8f42-27485091ccf2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299174}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ce9f87c1-fef4-5477-8a7a-149b90b7f486" :question/math-academy-id "q-317530" :question/problem "For the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y-2x &=9 \\\\ -5y\\, &=-15,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nits representation using matrices is\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-1}}</td><td>{{field-2}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-3}}</td><td>$-5$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>$x$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$y$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>$9$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-4}}</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$.$</span>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that it is in the correct order and both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+y &=9 \\\\ 0x-5y &=-15\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -15\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -15\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299618 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4594da98-1c2a-54d9-8a10-751dc6d6a248" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297837}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297837} :answer-field/id #uuid "10cf71a3-1902-5e22-a831-1fd47e406b59" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298697} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c8b4bec-ca96-58d1-b394-40b30e168da4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298237}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298237} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa5be443-392a-5f65-a6a9-f11df9b70cc9" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299212} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fe58c66-d1d9-590f-a96b-927875901a80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297623}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297623} :answer-field/id #uuid "b89b4d3f-1939-5756-b8ce-99a1e27fc048" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299261} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3e2b4b0-4685-5ae3-bafc-e5d93e75a043" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298584}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298584} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce53df6e-e873-51c6-b370-bb132a5e6f60" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299330}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ee62c6ba-71ac-57ec-bfe8-410ce9e1a842" :question/math-academy-id "q-317536" :question/problem "For the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4y-x &=3 \\\\ 9y+2x &=5,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nits representation using matrices is\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-1}}</td><td>$4$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-2}}</td><td>{{field-3}}</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>$x$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$y$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-4}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$5$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$.$</span>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that it is in the correct order and both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-x+4y &=3 \\\\ 2x+9y &=5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299619 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dbb4dbdb-c501-59e8-a1dd-8b0bd23d0eb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298495}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298495} :answer-field/id #uuid "1389ccbd-1b7a-5cb1-88d4-2ed1133983fe" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298709} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4de79627-eef5-5970-8e2d-eb52b1f0edc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297875}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297875} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b31d414-76e7-5210-916c-0c91bb636d73" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298788} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee7737ea-f780-5480-b74d-28a0673efadb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298564}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298564} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ca17d4e-624f-5422-818c-6a97ee47e9d7" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299152} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb8f547b-4751-5ed3-a16b-868f68570f62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298624}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298624} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5360a1e-9e7d-5e50-a64b-89bdb7d29784" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299464}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "042fab86-9bc5-5bac-af22-a67d3b6956f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-317540" :question/problem "For the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4 &=x \\\\ -7 &=3+y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nits representation using matrices is\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>$1$</td><td>{{field-1}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-2}}</td><td>{{field-3}}</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>$x$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$y$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-4}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$-10$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$.$</span>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that it’s in the correct order and both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+0y &=4 \\\\ 0x+y &=-10\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299621 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "afa59dcb-f7ce-5c09-a4c8-22b3dd6c17f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-2y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298317}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298317} :answer-field/id #uuid "558975f8-6e41-52d2-a81c-63a261f8cee1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298926} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec1d54c2-8080-5c78-b74c-cea3bc22fc7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x-y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298556}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298556} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd39ba45-0c63-53b1-89a4-29f995bbc06a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299386}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d9d91921-5228-5fa0-a7a6-2fcbc61ddda4" :question/math-academy-id "q-317563" :question/problem "What is the system of equations represented by\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -4 \\\\ -6 & 12\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}16 \\\\ -18\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system of equations is\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<div class=\"matrix-system\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"System of equations\">\n<table aria-label=\"Equation rows\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-1}}</td><td>$=$</td><td>$\\hspace{0.167em}4$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-2}}</td><td>$=$</td><td>$\\hspace{0.167em}\\hspace{0.167em}3.$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "The $2\\times 2$ matrix encodes the coefficients of $x$ and $y$, and the $2\\times 1$ vector on the right gives the constants, so the system is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}8x-4y &=16 \\\\ -6x+12y &=-18\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nDividing the first equation by $4$ and the second by $-6$ gives the simplified system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-y &=4 \\\\ x-2y &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhich matches the entries shown above."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299622 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c13d0ca-65a8-51a3-a5d1-a0920f6683b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3x+2y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298017}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298017} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a629bbe-7d36-5b30-862e-39429be187c2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298885} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc7c405e-3476-5c14-a227-d3f55c63a900" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x-5y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298634}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298634} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d050fae-3c59-5211-82f2-626d6e3d2224" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298895}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "61031038-e22c-5885-b49a-a1823235ca68" :question/math-academy-id "q-317570" :question/problem "What is the system of equations represented by\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}11 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system of equations is\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<div class=\"matrix-system\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"System of equations\">\n<table aria-label=\"Equation rows\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-1}}</td><td>$=$</td><td>$11$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-2}}</td><td>$=$</td><td>$\\hspace{0.167em}\\hspace{0.167em}-7.$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "The $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x-5y &=11 \\\\ -3x+2y &=-7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299623 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c6aab5e-cd3c-5e96-95c4-087bae5528eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297865}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297865} :answer-field/id #uuid "477735a7-4ce2-51d0-ac73-6c78382c8e52" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298879} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc8e6f31-d8cc-59a5-a7c1-8733b1f94e29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298374}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298374} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8ccb8e1-1b38-53eb-8622-5c815d1d251a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299425}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b07676ec-4252-579f-89b9-78b9cf7c6870" :question/math-academy-id "q-317582" :question/problem "What is the system of equations represented by\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system of equations is\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<div class=\"matrix-system\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"System of equations\">\n<table aria-label=\"Equation rows\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-1}}</td><td>$=$</td><td>$5$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-2}}</td><td>$=$</td><td>$\\hspace{0.167em}\\hspace{0.167em}-7.$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "The  $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}0x+1y &=5 \\\\ -1x+0y &=-7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSimplifying both equations in the system, we get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=5 \\\\ -x &=-7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299624 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82829b2e-baf5-5fab-a903-a5316f8d9f1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3x+2y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298116}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298116} :answer-field/id #uuid "23562a54-29b9-5cdd-98d6-f06cb96d7dd5" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298753} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44d0b073-d74e-5949-bc02-d145609dc06c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297834}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297834} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2e2fcd2-15bf-58c4-b88d-698133875b26" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299407}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "267f94e4-48b2-5a54-9c3b-23086cc4a9c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-317583" :question/problem "What is the system of equations represented by\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system of equations is\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<div class=\"matrix-system\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"System of equations\">\n<table aria-label=\"Equation rows\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-1}}</td><td>$=$</td><td>$10$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-2}}</td><td>$=$</td><td>$\\hspace{0.167em}\\hspace{0.167em}-7.$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "The  $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x+0y &=10 \\\\ -3x+2y &=-7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSimplifying both equations in the system, we get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x &=10 \\\\ -3x+2y &=-7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299747 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4f2334d-4d19-5657-ae3e-4861480ed63d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298594}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298594} :answer-field/id #uuid "78b9513e-697d-5d7b-bee1-be7a3d121ec8" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299048} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bbfc66b-fff8-5004-b6dd-86427e259c6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297674}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297674} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0d77a70-66b2-5ffc-82b6-2ce4bec2f8bb" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299237} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90e59730-fbc2-5bbb-83ce-1f84517628d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298183}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298183} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9818ff9-bf1d-504a-a640-f403039467ce" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299378}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0876fd99-09ab-5402-abb3-c07e19b050b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-319360" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -4\\end{bmatrix}$\ngiven that $det(A)=-5.$\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">${A}^{-1}=-\\frac{1}{5}\\hspace{0.222em}\\hspace{0.222em}$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>$-17$</td><td>{{field-1}}</td><td>$-1$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$12$</td><td>{{field-2}}</td><td>$1$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$-3$</td><td>{{field-3}}</td><td>$1$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** We are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}4 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-17 & -12 & -3 \\\\ -4 & -4 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-17 & 12 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}-17 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 12 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}-17 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 12 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299749 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b1e8767-de2d-52c7-8e2b-c1d59dee9c2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298230}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298230} :answer-field/id #uuid "083d9e98-ca8d-5676-958b-ffeedf627de1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298664} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1899ba9d-d3c7-55ce-9eb0-e8c2dc7a4673" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297659}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297659} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e3ce860-5116-5e9b-8117-529c03e68d73" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298901} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5975fdb6-cb9e-539a-b015-6e5266540e3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297926}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297926} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8b9f6c6-8575-50de-8fb6-95b3ce4f2904" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299478}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "228d219f-a988-51e3-add6-8253de28fd6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-319370" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$\ngiven that $det(A)=-4.$\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">${A}^{-1}=-\\frac{1}{4}\\hspace{0.222em}\\hspace{0.222em}$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>$-1$</td><td>{{field-1}}</td><td>$1$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$4$</td><td>{{field-2}}</td><td>$0$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$7$</td><td>{{field-3}}</td><td>$1$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** We are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -4 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -9 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 4 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 9 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 9 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299750 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a46a2082-4701-5caa-8a18-53b0c4269a8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298274}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298274} :answer-field/id #uuid "598ac1fb-ed3b-5180-8cb1-1204c40529bd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298943} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66ae1504-4970-5613-87dc-94b7c840f849" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297990}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297990} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e4160be-bab1-5130-a5b3-baad952ec2d9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299062} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd4225cd-a6f9-5811-a080-99edbbbc07c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298445}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298445} :answer-field/id #uuid "b02672dc-f7e5-58dc-a2a8-072fe03a302b" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299233}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "74394102-8729-5a30-8d7e-62d8f0117047" :question/math-academy-id "q-319372" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$\ngiven that $det(A)=7.$\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{7}\\hspace{0.222em}\\hspace{0.222em}$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>$-1$</td><td>{{field-1}}</td><td>$-1$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$-11$</td><td>{{field-2}}</td><td>$3$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$-4$</td><td>{{field-3}}</td><td>$3$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** We are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 11 & -4 \\\\ -1 & -10 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -11 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -10 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -11 & -10 & 3 \\\\ -4 & -3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -11 & -10 & 3 \\\\ -4 & -3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299753 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9aca02af-1267-5495-8514-3c0b3c60eb1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298229}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298229} :answer-field/id #uuid "334b73ec-67fc-5e0a-a799-7aa8a5b37cd6" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298812} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43320049-f27b-50cd-97bc-171b22e5c4c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297824}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297824} :answer-field/id #uuid "78f99d59-45ab-5371-902e-8352a898486d" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299049} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e895a78-e9aa-58ba-aab5-2fa17cb12e1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297950}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297950} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b9d8fad-aa30-5871-84b3-b6f919b19455" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299150} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49aed189-4a5b-58cc-bc59-cee854ce956e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297854}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297854} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ece9237-745d-5b97-a4df-453863812eaa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299163}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ca1a8117-1d26-5acd-beac-beb6e4c1cfa3" :question/math-academy-id "q-319395" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">${A}^{-1}=\\hspace{0.222em}\\hspace{0.222em} {{field-2}}$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>$-1$</td><td>$-3$</td><td>{{field-1}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$-1$</td><td>$3$</td><td>{{field-3}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$0$</td><td>{{field-4}}</td><td>$3$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** Find the determinant of $A.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & =(-3)\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{vmatrix}-0\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix}+1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-3)(2-3)-0(\\,-2-(-3)\\,)+(-3+3) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -9 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -9 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -9 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299754 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6598caed-bd43-5485-82fc-6172d6afee81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2/11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297986}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297986} :answer-field/id #uuid "87b160ba-8853-58cf-97da-7d8ad0eb9b07" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299093}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e7e72b45-0695-5b36-9476-7542514f8aaf" :question/math-academy-id "q-319409" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n${a}_{32}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{vmatrix} & =2\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{vmatrix}-0\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{vmatrix}+(-1)\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2(6-0)-0(-3-0)-1(1-0) \\\\  & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{32}^{t}={c}_{23}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{23} & =(-1)^{2+3}\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(2-0) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{32}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{32}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{23} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{11}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299756 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4ed675a-e374-5734-95e6-b38d1d46a8c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298339}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298339} :answer-field/id #uuid "9144a26f-d207-5329-a4f2-7e4b73ff0242" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299117}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e9cc9cf4-3e2c-5fa2-9cc3-9a41fb5db658" :question/math-academy-id "q-319413" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n${a}_{12}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & =2\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix}-0\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{vmatrix}+(-1)\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2(6-0)-0(-2-0)-1(1-0) \\\\  & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{12}^{t}={c}_{21}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{21} & =(-1)^{2+1}\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(0+1) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{12}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{12}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{21} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{11}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299757 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08bb5b15-8035-5a87-b994-7a63a290fd15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5/13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297598}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297598} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a8cea55-04b6-5a91-988e-863b5a98418a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298947}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8dd1f6d6-3609-5dae-86b5-57186f677ef3" :question/math-academy-id "q-319416" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{33}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n${a}_{33}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & =1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{vmatrix}-(-2)\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix}+0\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(2-(-3))+2(4-0)+0(6-0) \\\\  & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{33}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{33}^{t}={c}_{33}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{33} & =(-1)^{3+3}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =+\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(1+4) \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{33}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{33}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{33} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{13}\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
